- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'
  curator: edison_literature_identity
  action: ANNOTATED
  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Vitamin_B-edison-literature.md
    (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather
    than linked). Report verdict: **Recommendation: retain `UNMAPPED` and `UNDEFINED_MIXTURE`.**
    The bare label **“Vitamin B” is not a single chemical identity**. In modern nomenclature,
    the B complex comprises eight distinct vitamins: B1/thiamine, B2/riboflavin, B3/niacin,
    B5/pantothenic acid, B6/pyridoxine-family vitamers, B7/biotin, B9/folate, and
    B12/cobalamins. These compounds do not share one molecular formula, salt state,
    c CURIEs discussed: NCIT:C944. Recorded as provenance only — no grounding applied
    from this run. Edison''s recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a
    plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what
    #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s to accept or reject.'
  llm_assisted: true
- timestamp: '2026-08-30T06:20:04.233651+00:00'
  curator: claude_culturemech_alias_backfill
  action: ADDED_SYNONYMS
  changes: 'Added 2 CultureMech recipe surface form(s) that folded onto this record''s
